From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:26:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btmt6797: set up voice links with the older
 command

The controller lists Enhanced Setup Synchronous Connection, and uses it
for CVSD, but refuses transparent air mode through it with status 0x20.
The command fails before any link attempt, so the core has no fallback
and mSBC never comes up. Setup Synchronous Connection with voice setting
0x0063 and the same T2 values gives an eSCO link with air mode 3.

Mark Enhanced Setup as broken, so the core uses the older command for
every voice link. Which parameter the controller objects to stays open.
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c
index 3559f4f95..9c425f774 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c
@@ -212,6 +212,8 @@ static int btmt6797_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_NON_PERSISTENT_SETUP);
 	hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_RESET_ON_CLOSE);
 	hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_MWS_TRANSPORT_CONFIG);
+	/* Refuses transparent air mode, which the older command accepts. */
+	hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_ENHANCED_SETUP_SYNC_CONN);
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, bt);
 	ret = hci_register_dev(hdev);
 	if (ret < 0)
-- 
